{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Invariants","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Submodule","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GroupAlgebraCenter","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GramNondegenerate","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Character","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Contraction","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.card_le_card_conjClasses_of_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.card_le_card_conjClasses_of_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L300-L323","doc":"**The count.**  A family of class functions that is orthogonal with nonzero\ndiagonal for `charForm` is no larger than the number of conjugacy classes.\n\nApplied to the characters of pairwise non-isomorphic simple modules, this is\n`#simples ≤ #conj classes`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm_charOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm_charOf","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L290-L296","doc":"`charForm` computes `dim Hom_G` on characters — `charPairing_eq_finrank_homG`\nrestated for the bilinear form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L285-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charForm","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L271-L283","doc":"The character pairing as a bilinear form on all of `G → k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.stable_eq_bot_or_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.stable_eq_bot_or_top","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L238-L254","doc":"**`IsSimpleModule` over `k[G]` gives the stable-subspace form.**  Mathlib's\n`Representation.mapSubmodule` is an order isomorphism between the invariant\n`k`-submodules and the `k[G]`-submodules, so simplicity transports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.one_le_finrank_homG_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.one_le_finrank_homG_self","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L225-L236","doc":"The identity is always an equivariant self-map, so `Hom_G(V, V)` is nonzero\nwhenever `V` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.homG_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.homG_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L198-L223","doc":"**Schur's lemma.** If every `G`-stable subspace of `V` and of `W` is trivial\nand the two are not isomorphic as representations, there is no nonzero\nequivariant map `V → W`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charPairing_eq_finrank_homG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charPairing_eq_finrank_homG","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L173-L188","doc":"**The character pairing computes `dim Hom_G(V, W)`.**\n\n  `⅟|G| • Σ_g χ_V(g⁻¹) · χ_W(g) = dim_k Hom_G(V, W)`\n\nNo algebraically closed field, and no `Simple` hypothesis: this is the general\nidentity from which both the vanishing on non-isomorphic simples and the nonzero\ndiagonal are read off. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.mem_homG_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.mem_homG_iff","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L160-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.homG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.homG","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L154-L158","doc":"The space of `G`-equivariant `k`-linear maps `V → W`, as a submodule of\n`V →ₗ[k] W`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.average_charOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.average_charOf","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**`⅟|G| • Σ_g χ_ρ(g) = dim_k ρ^G`.**  `FDRep.average_char_eq_finrank_invariants`\nwithout the category layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_linHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_linHom","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L94-L124","doc":"**`χ_{Hom(V,W)}(g) = χ_V(g⁻¹) · χ_W(g)`.**\n\nThe trace is moved across `dualTensorHomEquiv` with `trace_comp_comm'` rather\nthan `trace_conj'`: the latter needs `Module.End k (V* ⊗ W)` unified with\n`(V* ⊗ W) →ₗ[k] (V* ⊗ W)`, which sends `isDefEq` into `dualTensorHomEquiv`'s\ndefinition and does not terminate within a million heartbeats. Composites keep\neverything at the `→ₗ` level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.linHom_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.linHom_comp","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L83-L92","doc":"`dualTensorHom` intertwines `dual ρV ⊗ ρW` with `linHom ρV ρW` — the\n`∘ₗ` form of `Representation.dualTensorHom_comm`, kept as composites rather than\nas a `LinearEquiv.conj` because the conjugation form makes `isDefEq` unfold\n`dualTensorHomEquiv` and diverge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_conj","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L61-L65","doc":"Characters are class functions: `tr` is conjugation-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf_apply","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter.charOf","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RepresentationCharacter.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The **character** of a representation: `g ↦ tr (ρ g)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}